<onlyinclude>A '''semiconductor foundry''' is a factory business that makes chips designed by other companies. The customer provides the chip design; the foundry uses specialized equipment to manufacture many copies on silicon wafers. A company that designs chips without owning its own fabrication plant is called ''fabless''.</onlyinclude>

== How it works ==
A chip designer chooses a manufacturing process and follows the foundry's design rules. After the design passes checks, the foundry makes the patterned wafer. The individual chips are then separated, packaged and tested through the relevant manufacturing partners.

== Why it matters ==
Chip factories require expensive equipment and highly controlled processes. Sharing a foundry lets multiple design companies use that infrastructure without building their own factories. A chip design that works in simulation may still fail manufacturing tests, so the foundry and designer coordinate on rules, verification and production yield.

